jobs.description:
Join us and celebrate the beauty of human experience. Create for happier, healthier lives, with love for nature. Together, with kindness, humility, and a spirit of adventure, we deliver food innovations, craft inspired fragrances and develop beauty and wellbeing solutions. There’s much to learn from our 79 production sites worldwide, known for their best-in-class processes and procedures. There’s many to learn from, with high-performing leaders and caring colleagues to explore ideas and ambitions with. Every day, your energy, your personality, and your determination will shape our future, making a positive difference on billions of people. Every essence of you enriches our world. We are Givaudan. Human by nature.

As an **Innovation Project Intern (m/f/d)**, you will directly report to our Innovation Project Manager. You will join our Operations Innovation Team in **Vernier (Geneva)**for an internship of **6-9 months.**

During this paid internship, you will contribute to innovation projects focused on modular automation, AI and data analytics, intra-logistics, robotics, and latest manufacturing technologies. You will combine technical project work with project coordination. You will support activities ranging from early technology assessment and prototype testing to data analysis, supplier coordination, project documentation, and presentations management.

This internship offers a unique opportunity to gain hands-on exposure to industrial innovation projects while supporting the development of scalable manufacturing solutions.

## In this exciting role you will:

- Support innovation projects from early concept evaluation through experimentation, pilot implementation and validation;
- Conduct technology, market and supplier research related to automation, robotics, AI, data analytics, intra-logistics and new manufacturing technologies;
- Help prepare user requirements, functional requirements and solution specifications;
- Contribute to high-level system architecture and integration discussions;
- Support the planning and execution of prototype testing, experiments and pilot activities;
- Develop and execute test protocols to evaluate solution performance, reliability, efficiency and technical feasibility;
- Work hands-on with prototypes, automation equipment, robots, sensors and experimental setups
- Collect, structure, clean and analyze technical and operational data;
- Identify and document technical risks, improvement opportunities and lessons learned during testing and pilot activities;
- Support supplier coordination, technical discussions, action resolution of open points;
- Present technical findings, project updates and recommendations to project managers and other partners
- Support project planning, action tracking, meeting preparation and follow-up activities.

